# `services/` is reserved for long-running daemons that wrap a single
# `@melandlabs/*` package as a deployable server. Example services:
#
# - `services/memory-http`  — `opencontext-memory-http` daemon (Hono on :7421)
# - `services/memory-mcp`   — `opencontext-memory-mcp` stdio MCP server
#
# Each service should be a thin wrapper that:
#   1. Imports the relevant `@melandlabs/*` package
#   2. Adds a CLI front-end (commander, yargs, or @clack/prompts)
#   3. Adds operational concerns (logging, signal handling, config)
#
# Avoid re-implementing business logic in services — that belongs in
# the underlying package.